# CREDITS — The Dry Stair

A 40-second film in the Silkscreen Travel Poster style, made entirely in code.
Brine Stair, the hour, and the ticket window are invented. No real coast, park, agency, or poster is portrayed.

## Voice
Speech synthesis: Kokoro (kokoro-onnx), voice `af_heart`, English. Model and engine
are released under the licences of the kokoro-onnx project
(https://github.com/thewh1teagle/kokoro-onnx). Offline synthesis.

## Music
Original score, written for this film (`music/score.py`).
Nylon guitar and pizzicato bass are physically modelled (`core/audio/pluck.py`).
Brushes and the harmonica reed are synthesised in the same file. No sample library.

## Typefaces
- Cormorant Garamond — SIL Open Font License 1.1, Christian Thalmann (Catharsis Fonts). See `fonts/OFL.txt`.
  The face is horizontally scaled in the picture so the names read condensed.

## Picture
Every frame is drawn with this film's silkscreen engine (`engine/silk.js`, `scene.js`).
No stock footage, no photographs, no third-party images.

## Sound effects
The squeegee, ink squelch, screen clack, hinge creak, clamp, stamps, room, paper hiss,
and surf are synthesised for this film (`mix.py`). No recorded effects.
